.SH "نام (NAME)"
lr_cron \- run the perodical jobs configured in a DlfStore.
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBlr_cron\fR \fIperiod\fR \fIstore\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBlr_cron\fR is designed to be called in a \fBcrontab\fR\|(5) entry.
\&\fIperiod\fR should be "hourly", "daily", "weekly", "monthly" or "yearly".
\&\fIstore\fR should be the full path name of the DLF Store.
.PP
\&\fBlire\fR\|(1) should be used to configure periodical jobs in the store.
.PP
To run jobs as scheduled by \fBlire\fR\|(1), you will need to setup cron jobs. For each
schedule you use, you should configure a cron job to be executed according to
that period.
.PP
Here is a \fBcrontab\fR\|(5) entry that will make sure that all possible
schedules are supported in the /home/flacoste/myStore DLF store:
.PP
.Vb 5
\& 05  *  *  *  * lr_run lr_cron hourly  /home/flacoste/myStore
\& 15 01  *  *  * lr_run lr_cron daily   /home/flacoste/myStore
\& 15 02  *  * 02 lr_run lr_cron weekly  /home/flacoste/myStore
\& 15 03 01  *  * lr_run lr_cron monthly /home/flacoste/myStore
\& 15 04 01  01 * lr_run lr_cron yearly  /home/flacoste/myStore
.Ve
.PP
\&.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBlire\fR\|(1)
